.TH geectl-branch-branch-package 1  "geectl-branch-branch-package 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-branch\-branch\-package \- Branch a package: create a linked copy under a branch project. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl branch branch\-package\fR [\fB\-\-target\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-target\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-devel\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-new\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-revision\fR] [\fB\-\-linkrev\fR] [\fB\-\-comment\fR] [\fB\-\-noaccess\fR] [\fB\-\-add\-repositories\fR] [\fB\-\-add\-repositories\-block\fR] [\fB\-\-add\-repositories\-rebuild\fR] [\fB\-\-extend\-package\-names\fR] [\fB\-\-maintenance\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-project\fR> <\fB\-\-package\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Branch a package: create a linked copy under a branch project. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the branch
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
The project to branch from
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
The package to branch
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-project\fR \fI<TARGET_PROJECT>\fR
The branch project. Without it, the server picks the default (usually `home:<user>:branches:<source project>`)
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-package\fR \fI<TARGET_PACKAGE>\fR
The branch package name. Without it, the source package name
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-devel\-project\fR
Ignore the devel project when resolving the link source
.TP
\fB\-\-new\-package\fR
Branch a package that does not exist yet
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite an existing target package
.TP
\fB\-\-revision\fR \fI<REVISION>\fR
Branch from this source revision instead of the latest
.TP
\fB\-\-linkrev\fR \fI<LINKREV>\fR
The link revision the branch records
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fI<COMMENT>\fR
A comment recorded on the branch
.TP
\fB\-\-noaccess\fR
Withhold the branch\*(Aqs read access to the source package\*(Aqs project
.TP
\fB\-\-add\-repositories\fR
Add the source project\*(Aqs repositories to the branch project
.TP
\fB\-\-add\-repositories\-block\fR \fI<ADD_REPOSITORIES_BLOCK>\fR
Block the added repositories. Only sent with `\-\-add\-repositories` (clap refuses it without that flag: a block the live run would silently drop must fail at parse time, not vanish)
.TP
\fB\-\-add\-repositories\-rebuild\fR \fI<ADD_REPOSITORIES_REBUILD>\fR
Rebuild the added repositories. Only sent with `\-\-add\-repositories` (clap refuses it without that flag, as above)
.TP
\fB\-\-extend\-package\-names\fR
Extend the branch package names with the source project name
.TP
\fB\-\-maintenance\fR
Branch as a maintenance incident
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
